WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.774
The architecture has two major parts:
coarse-to-fine visual-language reasoning for the answer,

00:00:05.854 --> 00:00:08.079
and an explanation generation module.

00:00:08.159 --> 00:00:13.560
A pre-trained Faster-RCNN extracts
region-of-interest features and image predicates such

00:00:13.640 --> 00:00:15.490
as object and attribute labels,

00:00:15.570 --> 00:00:17.359
which are embedded with GloVe.

00:00:17.439 --> 00:00:21.532
The question is encoded with GloVe embeddings
passed through a GRU,

00:00:21.612 --> 00:00:25.642
and question predicates are extracted by filtering
out stop words.

00:00:25.722 --> 00:00:29.628
These signals flow through three modules:
information filtering,

00:00:29.708 --> 00:00:33.365
which removes noisy region information; multimodal
learning,

00:00:33.445 --> 00:00:39.718
which uses bilinear attention networks to fuse
image and question at both coarse and fine granularity;

00:00:39.798 --> 00:00:44.513
and semantic reasoning, which combines the two
levels into a joint embedding.

00:00:44.593 --> 00:00:51.800
That joint embedding is sent both to a multi-layer
perceptron for answer prediction and to the explanation generator.

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:54.292
Two generator architectures are studied,

00:00:54.372 --> 00:00:57.717
a two-layer LSTM and an eight-head Transformer decoder,

00:00:57.797 --> 00:01:04.007
each trained with autoregressive cross-entropy loss
and teacher forcing on ground-truth explanations.

00:01:04.087 --> 00:01:09.550
The whole system is trained end-to-end with a
combined loss that balances the answer term

00:01:09.630 --> 00:01:12.540
and the explanation term through a factor alpha.
